#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5e98ebc-02bd-54b5-a757-d065e8851467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+1\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341779} {:answer/id #uuid "27c16c28-2efc-5404-8a79-de11da720c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341780} {:answer/id #uuid "a302ec84-8b84-57a3-bfde-e52507cab31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341781} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb240ef-bc86-5d2c-981e-a1a0eb5dfad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341782} {:answer/id #uuid "d566978b-f262-5a4e-ad6f-2d7f8dfe7791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d566978b-f262-5a4e-ad6f-2d7f8dfe7791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341783} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3bfb3e0-02eb-584b-b143-02af187f4a8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9debd0df-2771-5276-9781-4c4c107557fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-11357" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+7$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{C}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+7)(x+1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+17 & =(Ax+B)(x+1)+C({x}^{2}+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=-1,B=3,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}=\\frac{-x+3}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{2}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{-x+3}{{x}^{2}+7}+\\frac{2}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use a substitution $u={x}^{2}+7.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+7| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}}).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+17}{({x}^{2}+7)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+7}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+7)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{7}}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{7}})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5015d66-9cb8-5042-b24a-739c400c11e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341786} {:answer/id #uuid "1c444fcc-2f83-52bf-ae5f-99d3c3e3b388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341787} {:answer/id #uuid "f376ef23-3066-5780-8a61-5fbc84f4c633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341788} {:answer/id #uuid "9a12247b-8a10-5efa-9c8f-0f464114e935" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341789} {:answer/id #uuid "e97a06ab-412f-56dd-af2a-09333c17849a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c444fcc-2f83-52bf-ae5f-99d3c3e3b388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341787} :answer-field/id #uuid "80ec4059-883c-5d8c-94b5-eb3aeb5102dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99798b4d-8a0a-5c2b-888b-3cedc5021d58" :question/math-academy-id "q-115686" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}.$" :question/worked-solution "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+1$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{C}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+1)(x-4),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-9x+5 & =(Ax+B)(x-4)+C({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=-1,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)} & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+3.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+1| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63df8e8a-de87-5f04-94ba-1adeaa275a29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341793} {:answer/id #uuid "2026753c-2a95-516a-8e36-a8b45a756c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341794} {:answer/id #uuid "68de0c6b-840f-50fe-8dfa-9a0944c1edb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341795} {:answer/id #uuid "367e2e6e-aa98-522f-8acb-9b4997e4dbe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341796} {:answer/id #uuid "f320924a-a119-5145-bb90-6cd098e55ba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68de0c6b-840f-50fe-8dfa-9a0944c1edb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341795} :answer-field/id #uuid "75d6192b-2fda-552b-b654-d948c73582f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a13ff449-7069-519d-95f0-893e15f21aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-115710" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral  $\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD=(4)^{2}-4(1)(-6)=40\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{40}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x({x}^{2}+4x-6),$ and we get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+12x-12=A({x}^{2}+4x-6)+(Bx+C)x\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=2$, and $C=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+4x-6.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(2x+4)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b3faeb1-f4ef-52b9-89c6-69902cf18d33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341800} {:answer/id #uuid "8096737b-b3ed-5d19-93e6-aef7bf70d66a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341801} {:answer/id #uuid "89f31892-3807-598f-9dbb-13ba441d6917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341802} {:answer/id #uuid "d59685b8-c6c4-5989-a41d-30bdd1f251df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341803} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b453c0-81cc-5521-bd9e-9f51f1f11721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8096737b-b3ed-5d19-93e6-aef7bf70d66a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341801} :answer-field/id #uuid "aace1bc0-4029-56bd-83f2-c490e8c58495" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb88ac70-729c-5c15-8fad-c3a30aa15d49" :question/math-academy-id "q-3615" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a negative discriminant:\n\n$$\nD=(-2)^{2}-4(1)(3)=-8<0\n$$\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}+\\frac{C}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-3 & =(Ax+B)(x+1)+C({x}^{2}-2x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get  $A=\\frac{3}{2},$ $B=-\\frac{3}{2},$ and $C=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}=\\frac{3x-3}{2({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{2(x+1)}.\n$$\n\nNow we integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration only at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3x-3}{2({x}^{2}-2x+3)}-\\frac{1}{2(x+1)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}-2x+3.$ Then $(2x-2)\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-2x+3| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x-3}{({x}^{2}-2x+3)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{{x}^{2}-2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-2x+3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7de5944-ca6c-5936-b830-3186d1191883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2({x}^{2}-4x-3)}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341807} {:answer/id #uuid "361a06f0-d2c9-5cf7-bc54-13df424db387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341808} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc39e85-8e72-5152-9358-6ff1ac3cd0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341809} {:answer/id #uuid "60a42eec-a246-5362-b524-6ca583c5aa2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341810} {:answer/id #uuid "005d3e0f-d3f5-5419-8f5d-7a5989ee0002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbc39e85-8e72-5152-9358-6ff1ac3cd0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341809} :answer-field/id #uuid "aad8a85d-a67d-5b0d-85f4-b57b947ee73c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5fc9280-fa79-5c2f-95ea-95a92d8c6c5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-83367" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD=(-4)^{2}-4(1)(-3)=28\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{28}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}=\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-3x-9=A({x}^{2}-4x-3)+(Bx+C)(x+3)\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=1,B=1$ and $C=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}=\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}-4x-3.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2(x-2)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
